    "name":  "Left testicular pain",
    "module":  "male-genital",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Left testicular pain refers to pain perceived in or around the left testicle. Clinically it is managed identically to right testicular pain. Important causes include left testicular torsion (surgical emergency), epididymo-orchitis, varicocele (more common on the left due to the angle of the left spermatic vein draining into the left renal vein), trauma, hernia, and testicular tumour. A left varicocele that does not decompress in the supine position should raise suspicion for a retroperitoneal mass compressing the left renal vein.",
